1	# REFERENCE — verified on this machine on 2026-10-24
2	Node v20.20.1, npm 10.8.2, Docker 29.1.3. Working project: /home/electronica-care/ezy-prep/dryrun/app
3	Versions that worked: Next 16.4.3, React 19.3.0, Prisma 7.10.1, @prisma/client 7.10.1 (+ @prisma/adapter-pg 7.10.1, pg), @supabase/ssr 0.12.7, @supabase/supabase-js 2.118.0, supabase CLI 2.122.0, Vitest 4.1.12, shadcn 4.22.1 (style base-nova), Tailwind 4.3.3, ESLint 9.39.5, TS 5.9.3.
4	Prisma schemas setting that db pull accepted: `schemas = ["auth", "public"]` (public-only FAILS with P4002 because memberships.user_id -> auth.users).
5	
6	## Setup commands that worked, in order
7	```bash
8	npx --yes create-next-app@16 app --ts --app --src-dir --tailwind --eslint --no-turbopack --import-alias "@/*" --use-npm --yes
9	cd app
10	npx supabase@2.122.0 init && sed -i 's/^project_id = "app"/project_id = "<name>"/' supabase/config.toml
11	npx supabase@2.122.0 start            # run in background; continue with installs meanwhile
12	echo 'node-options=--experimental-websocket' > .npmrc     # GOTCHA 1, do before anything runs supabase-js
13	npm i @prisma/client@7.10.1 @prisma/adapter-pg@7.10.1 pg @supabase/ssr @supabase/supabase-js
14	npm i -D prisma@7.10.1 @types/pg dotenv
15	npm i -D vitest@4 --legacy-peer-deps                     # GOTCHA 2 + 3
16	npx prisma init --datasource-provider postgresql         # writes prisma7.config.ts, prisma/schema.prisma, .env
17	npx --yes shadcn@latest init -y -d                       # also creates components/ui/button.tsx
18	npx shadcn@latest add button -y
19	npm pkg set scripts.postinstall="prisma generate" scripts.test="vitest run" scripts.typecheck="tsc --noEmit"
20	# write .env from supabase (overwrite the prisma placeholder):
21	eval "$(npx supabase status -o env 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^(API_URL|ANON_KEY|SERVICE_ROLE_KEY|DB_URL)=')"
22	printf 'NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=%s\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=%s\nSUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=%s\nDATABASE_URL=%s\n' "$API_URL" "$ANON_KEY" "$SERVICE_ROLE_KEY" "$DB_URL" > .env
23	# add migration supabase/migrations/20261024000001_init.sql + supabase/seed.sql, then:
24	npx supabase db reset                 # if it says DbSetupError "exit 1" right after start: just rerun
25	# add schemas = ["auth","public"] to datasource, then:
26	npx prisma db pull && npx prisma generate
27	npx tsc --noEmit && npx eslint . --max-warnings=0 && npm run build
28	for tz in UTC Asia/Dubai America/New_York; do TZ=$tz npx vitest run; done
29	npx supabase stop
30	```
31	`supabase status -o env` names: API_URL (http://127.0.0.1:54321), REST_URL, DB_URL (…:54322/postgres), STUDIO_URL (:54323), MAILPIT_URL (:54324), ANON_KEY, SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, PUBLISHABLE_KEY (sb_publishable_…), SECRET_KEY (sb_secret_…), JWT_SECRET.
32	
33	## Timing (this machine, cold caches)
34	create-next-app ~7 min (npm install), supabase start first time ~19 min (image pulls; ~1 min once images cached), npm installs ~5 min, shadcn ~40 s. Steps 1–6 wall-clock ≈ 32 min. **Start `supabase start` in background first**; images are now cached on this machine.
35	
36	## Gotchas + fixes
37	1. **supabase-js 2.118 on Node 20 throws `Node.js detected but native WebSocket not found`** at createClient (node scripts, vitest). Fix: `.npmrc` with `node-options=--experimental-websocket` (applies to npm run / npx), or `node --experimental-websocket script.mjs`. The Next server (dev/start) worked without it.
38	2. **vitest 5 requires Node >=22** → use `vitest@4` (4.1.12).
39	3. `npm i -D vitest` fails with `Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')` (npm 10.8.2 bug on optional peer jsdom→canvas). Fix: `--legacy-peer-deps` (once; later plain `npm i` works).
40	4. **`npm i prisma` installs 8.0.0-rc.27** (npm `latest` tag is an RC) while @prisma/client latest is 7.10.1. Pin both: `prisma@7.10.1 @prisma/client@7.10.1`.
41	5. Prisma 7: no `url` in schema.prisma; URL lives in config; client needs driver adapter (`@prisma/adapter-pg`); generator `prisma-client` with output `../src/generated/prisma`, import from `@/generated/prisma/client`. `prisma init` writes **prisma7.config.ts** (legacy `prisma.config.ts` is still accepted). It also drops agent skill dirs (.agents/.claude/.windsurf, skills-lock.json) — gitignored them.
42	6. `prisma db pull` with default (public only): P4002 cross-schema reference to auth.users → `schemas = ["auth","public"]` (pulls ~27 auth models + enums; fine). Models get `@@schema("public")`.
43	7. First `supabase db reset` right after start failed `DbSetupError: error running container: exit 1`; rerun succeeded.
44	8. vitest.config: `import { loadEnvConfig } from "@next/env"` fails in .mts (CJS) → `import nextEnv from "@next/env"; nextEnv.loadEnvConfig(process.cwd())`. Use `vitest.config.mts` (a .ts config warns about ESM-as-CJS).
45	9. Top-level await in a tsx script: name it `.mts` (`npx --yes tsx scripts/prisma-check.mts`).
46	10. create-next-app 16 sets `cacheComponents: true` in next.config.ts; /api/me with cookies() still built as dynamic (ƒ) — no change needed. AGENTS.md says read node_modules/next/dist/docs/.
47	11. ESLint: Next 16 flat config (`eslint.config.mjs`, defineConfig + globalIgnores) passed `--max-warnings=0` unchanged; added `"src/generated/**"` to globalIgnores (not strictly needed).
48	12. create-next-app `.gitignore` has `.env*` (would ignore .env.example) → replace with `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env*.local`, `!.env.example`; check `git ls-files .env.example`.
49	13. `postinstall: prisma generate` verified to succeed with no `.env` and no DATABASE_URL.
50	14. Kit says `vitest.config.ts`: a `.ts` config works but prints an ESM-as-CJS warning; `.mts` is clean (needs the default-import fix in 8).
51	15. Don't `pkill -f 'next start'` from a shell whose command line contains that string — kills itself. Kill by pid from `ss -ltnp | grep :3000`.
52	
